le `tls_api_one_scenario_init_ex` function in util.rs. So I need to map the parameters from the C `_ex2` call to what's available in the Rust version. ALPN and SNI, which `tls_api_one_scenario_init_ex` doesn't expose. So there may need to be a new helper, or we use `tls_api_one_scenario_init_ex` and accept the difference.\n\nThe app_limited test needs a different initialization path because it uses custom callbacks and specific ALPN settings. Looking at how similar tests work, `tls_api_one_scenario_init_ex` accepts `Version` and optional `ConnectionId`, while the C variant also handles ALPN and SNI. I should add a `tls_api_init_ctx_ex2` helper function to `tests/util.rs` to handle this, since the constraints allow adding helpers there and I can't modify `Cargo.toml` or files outside `rs/fq/`.\n\nFor the app_limited test itself, I need to implement the custom callback that enforces rate-limited streaming... I need to understand the `StreamDataCallback` trait interface to implement it properly for the app_limited context. The C test uses a shared callback with an `is_server` flag, but the Rust approach would benefit from separate implementations for client and server sides. Let me focus on what actually needs to be translated versus what can be stubbed out for now.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":688,"cache_read_input_tokens":53031,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":688},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b2f5f784-a6db-4c71-b3d0-86f74527db79","uuid":"dc5e3da3-b0a7-4d78-9463-220fb104fd20"}
