{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AirgRhHWaM6c6npLd4Fv7H","type":"tool_result","content":"410\t\n411\t/// Event type passed to the application's stream / connection\n412\t/// callback (see [`StreamDataCallback`]).  Identifies which sort of\n413\t/// notification the stack is delivering — stream data, lifecycle\n414\t/// transition, datagram event, path event, etc.\n415\t#[derive(Debug, Copy, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\n416\tpub enum CallbackEvent {\n417\t    StreamData = 0,\n418\t    StreamFin,\n419\t    StreamReset,\n420\t    StopSending,\n421\t    StatelessReset,\n422\t    Close,\n423\t    ApplicationClose,\n424\t    StreamGap,\n425\t    PrepareToSend,\n426\t    AlmostReady,\n427\t    Ready,\n428\t    Datagram,\n429\t    VersionNegotiation,\n430\t    RequestAlpnList,\n431\t    SetAlpn,\n432\t    PacingChanged,\n433\t    PrepareDatagram,\n434\t    DatagramAcked,\n435\t    DatagramLost,\n436\t    DatagramSpurious,\n437\t    PathAvailable,\n438\t    PathSuspended,\n439\t    PathDeleted,\n440\t    PathQualityChanged,\n441\t    PathAddressObserved,\n442\t    AppWakeup,\n443\t    NextPathAllowed,\n444\t}\n445\t\n446\t// Transport-parameter shapes live in [`crate::tp`].\n447\t\n448\t// Stream-id decomposition lives on [`crate::stream::StreamId`].\n449\t\n450\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n451\t// Time management.\n452\t\n453\t/// Wall-clock microseconds since the Unix epoch.\n454\t///\n455\t/// The C body reads the OS clock; in Rust this requires the `std`\n456\t/// feature (`std::time::SystemTime`).  The `cfg`-gated split lands\n457\t/// when the crate gains its `std` feature and the rest of the\n458\t/// `no_std + alloc` plumbing — for Phase 1 the function is just a\n459\t/// `todo!()` stub.\n460\tpub fn current_time() -> u64 {\n461\t    todo!()\n462\t}\n463\t\n464\timpl Quic {\n465\t    /// Virtual time used by this QUIC context (wall-clock or\n466\t    /// simulated, depending on whether a simulated-time pointer was\n467\t    /// supplied at creation).  C: `get_quic_time`.\n468\t    pub fn time(&self) -> u64 {\n469\t        todo!()\n470\t    }\n471\t}\n472\t\n473\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n474\t// Application callbacks (function-pointer typedefs → traits).\n475\t\n476\t/// Stream/event callback installed on a QUIC context or connection.\n477\t/// Folds the C `void* callback_ctx` into the trait implementor's\n478\t/// state; `stream_ctx` is per-stream and remains a raw pointer\n479\t/// because it is produced and consumed by the application without\n480\t/// the stack interpreting it.\n481\t///\n482\t/// Returns the C `int` directly: `0` for success, or one of the\n483\t/// `_*` codes (e.g. `STREAM_RECEIVE_COMPLETE`) for\n484\t/// special signalling.  Phase 3 may refine to `Result` once the\n485\t/// crate-level error type lands.\n486\t///\n487\t/// `bytes` is `&[u8]` rather than `*const u8 + size_t`; events that\n488\t/// carry no payload pass `&[]`.\n489\tpub trait StreamDataCallback {\n490\t    fn callback(\n491\t        &mut self,\n492\t        connection: &mut Connection,\n493\t        stream_id: u64,\n494\t        bytes: &[u8],\n495\t        fin_or_event: CallbackEvent,\n496\t        stream_ctx: Option<&mut dyn core::any::Any>,\n497\t    ) -> i32;\n498\t}\n499\t\n500\t/// ALPN-selection callback.  Returns the index of the chosen ALPN\n501\t/// in `list`, or any value `>= list.len()` to signal \"none of the\n502\t/// proposed ALPNs is supported\".  C: `AlpnSelect` (the C `_v2`\n503\t/// flavour is folded in — it only differed in the iovec type, which\n504\t/// is now just `&[u8]`).\n505\t/// Application hook the TLS backend invokes to choose one of the\n506\t/// client's proposed ALPN values.  Returns the chosen index into\n507\t/// `list`, or `None` to reject the handshake.\n508\t///\n509\t/// `list` carries the raw bytes off the wire; mapping to the\n510\t/// strongly-typed [`Alpn`] enum is up to the implementor (most\n511\t/// applications keep a small whitelist by string identifier).\n512\tpub trait AlpnSelect {\n513\t    fn select(&mut self, quic: &mut Quic, list: &[&[u8]]) -> Option<usize>;\n514\t}\n515\t\n516\t/// Callback that produces a server-environment-compatible CID.\n517\t/// Folds the C `void* connection_id_cb_data` into the implementor's state.\n518\t/// C: `ConnectionIdCallback`.\n519\tpub trait ConnectionIdCallback {"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b2f5f784-a6db-4c71-b3d0-86f74527db79","uuid":"9a779789-1fa8-4035-8797-b2e00291f409","timestamp":"2026-05-04T21:23:17.321Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/rs/fq/src/lib.rs","content":"\n/// Event type passed to the application's stream / connection\n/// callback (see [`StreamDataCallback`]).  Identifies which sort of\n/// notification the stack is delivering — stream data, lifecycle\n/// transition, datagram event, path event, etc.\n#[derive(Debug, Copy, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum CallbackEvent {\n    StreamData = 0,\n    StreamFin,\n    StreamReset,\n    StopSending,\n    StatelessReset,\n    Close,\n    ApplicationClose,\n    StreamGap,\n    PrepareToSend,\n    AlmostReady,\n    Ready,\n    Datagram,\n    VersionNegotiation,\n    RequestAlpnList,\n    SetAlpn,\n    PacingChanged,\n    PrepareDatagram,\n    DatagramAcked,\n    DatagramLost,\n    DatagramSpurious,\n    PathAvailable,\n    PathSuspended,\n    PathDeleted,\n    PathQualityChanged,\n    PathAddressObserved,\n    AppWakeup,\n    NextPathAllowed,\n}\n\n// Transport-parameter shapes live in [`crate::tp`].\n\n// Stream-id decomposition lives on [`crate::stream::StreamId`].\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Time management.\n\n/// Wall-clock microseconds since the Unix epoch.\n///\n/// The C body reads the OS clock; in Rust this requires the `std`\n/// feature (`std::time::SystemTime`).  The `cfg`-gated split lands\n/// when the crate gains its `std` feature and the rest of the\n/// `no_std + alloc` plumbing — for Phase 1 the function is just a\n/// `todo!()` stub.\npub fn current_time() -> u64 {\n    todo!()\n}\n\nimpl Quic {\n    /// Virtual time used by this QUIC context (wall-clock or\n    /// simulated, depending on whether a simulated-time pointer was\n    /// supplied at creation).  C: `get_quic_time`.\n    pub fn time(&self) -> u64 {\n        todo!()\n    }\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Application callbacks (function-pointer typedefs → traits).\n\n/// Stream/event callback installed on a QUIC context or connection.\n/// Folds the C `void* callback_ctx` into the trait implementor's\n/// state; `stream_ctx` is per-stream and remains a raw pointer\n/// because it is produced and consumed by the application without\n/// the stack interpreting it.\n///\n/// Returns the C `int` directly: `0` for success, or one of the\n/// `_*` codes (e.g. `STREAM_RECEIVE_COMPLETE`) for\n/// special signalling.  Phase 3 may refine to `Result` once the\n/// crate-level error type lands.\n///\n/// `bytes` is `&[u8]` rather than `*const u8 + size_t`; events that\n/// carry no payload pass `&[]`.\npub trait StreamDataCallback {\n    fn callback(\n        &mut self,\n        connection: &mut Connection,\n        stream_id: u64,\n        bytes: &[u8],\n        fin_or_event: CallbackEvent,\n        stream_ctx: Option<&mut dyn core::any::Any>,\n    ) -> i32;\n}\n\n/// ALPN-selection callback.  Returns the index of the chosen ALPN\n/// in `list`, or any value `>= list.len()` to signal \"none of the\n/// proposed ALPNs is supported\".  C: `AlpnSelect` (the C `_v2`\n/// flavour is folded in — it only differed in the iovec type, which\n/// is now just `&[u8]`).\n/// Application hook the TLS backend invokes to choose one of the\n/// client's proposed ALPN values.  Returns the chosen index into\n/// `list`, or `None` to reject the handshake.\n///\n/// `list` carries the raw bytes off the wire; mapping to the\n/// strongly-typed [`Alpn`] enum is up to the implementor (most\n/// applications keep a small whitelist by string identifier).\npub trait AlpnSelect {\n    fn select(&mut self, quic: &mut Quic, list: &[&[u8]]) -> Option<usize>;\n}\n\n/// Callback that produces a server-environment-compatible CID.\n/// Folds the C `void* connection_id_cb_data` into the implementor's state.\n/// C: `ConnectionIdCallback`.\npub trait ConnectionIdCallback {","numLines":110,"startLine":410,"totalLines":2380}}}
