{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_011Nyct7ffiJU2oGVAGPrune","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to fix:\n1. `octets_sent` field unused - add it to `prepare_to_send` code or add `#[allow(dead_code)]` on the struct\n2. `stream0_bytes_sent_this_packet` unused - same\n3. Two explicit auto-deref warnings - change `&mut *borrow` to `&mut borrow`\n\nFor the dead_code issues: `octets_sent` is used in the C server's PrepareToSend callback to track how much data has been sent. Since we're deferring that to Phase 4, the field is set in `new` but never read. Similarly `stream0_bytes_sent_this_packet` is part of the rate-pacing logic.\n\n\nThe cleanest approach is to suppress the dead_code warnings with attributes on the structs themselves, since these fields are legitimately part of the faithful translation—they're just not fully utilized until the PrepareToSend implementation is completed in Phase 4.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":706,"cache_read_input_tokens":101117,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":706},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b2f5f784-a6db-4c71-b3d0-86f74527db79","uuid":"1b7264dd-2853-49c8-a789-537eff3563d2"}
